1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,480
Have you ever wondered how many

2
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:02,960
times your heart beats in a

3
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:03,580
single day?

4
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:05,960
An average adult heart beats around

5
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:09,180
100,000 times every 24 hours.

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,040
That's more than 35 million beats

7
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,540
a year!

8
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,200
But how does it keep working

9
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,000
without stopping?

10
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:17,320
Your heart has four chambers,

11
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,780
two atria and two ventricles.

12
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,940
They work together to receive blood

13
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,680
and pump it throughout your body.

14
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,780
A natural electrical signal generated by

15
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,080
a group of cells called the

16
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:30,980
sinoatrial node controls each heartbeat.

17
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:32,720
With every contraction,

18
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,460
your heart delivers oxygen-rich blood to

19
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,620
your organs and tissues.

20
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:40,820
It pumps approximately 7,500 liters of

21
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:42,060
blood every day!

22
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,260
And incredibly,

23
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,700
it continues doing this even while

24
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,280
you're sleeping.

25
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:49,040
So why are our guts called

26
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,020
the second brain?

27
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,560
Want to know the answer?

28
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,100
Watch our next video.

29
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:54,660
And don't forget to follow us

30
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:56,680
for more amazing facts about your

31
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:56,960
body.
